    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0689" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12637.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. President Carbajal’s delegates have just left for Vera Cruz, whence they
                    will proceed at once to Tampico with instructions to negotiate at any place
                    agreeable to the Constitutionalist delegates in order to save time. The change
                    of itinerary was forcibly adopted because there is a gap of nearly 200
                    kilometers this side of San Luis Potosí.</p>
                <p>The President would like to know as soon as possible the names of the
                    Constitutionalist delegates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
